1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,900
Kola ID: verify once, prove anywhere, stay unlinkable. Built on Midnight by Mbanya Dev

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:12,400
Every app re-checks the same person, at about US$1 to 1.35 a check

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:17,900
and keeps a copy of their ID that it then has to protect

4
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:23,400
An issuer checks a person once. Only a commitment goes on Midnight

5
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:28,900
Apps get a zero-knowledge yes against their public policy, plus a per-app nullifier

6
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,951
The main demo: the Kola KYC registry, also deployed on Midnight Preprod

7
00:00:33,101 --> 00:00:38,197
1. The registry admin approves Kumba Verify, a KYC provider, as an issuer

8
00:00:38,347 --> 00:00:44,485
2. Kumba Verify checks Manka (28) and Ebai (17) once, and issues credentials. Only commitments go on-chain

9
00:00:44,635 --> 00:00:50,772
3. Sawa Exchange publishes a public policy: 18+, CM/GH/KE/NG, sanctions screened in the last 90 days

10
00:00:50,922 --> 00:00:57,016
4. Manka proves she meets the policy. Sawa gets a yes and a nullifier, never her birth date

11
00:00:57,166 --> 00:01:02,251
5. A second Sawa account from Manka is refused: one person, one account

12
00:01:02,401 --> 00:01:07,473
7. Ebai is 17: refused, and Sawa learns nothing about his actual age

13
00:01:07,623 --> 00:01:12,515
The public ledger: issuer keys, commitments, policies and nullifiers. No names, no birth dates

14
00:01:12,666 --> 00:01:17,518
Beyond finance: the same contract, unchanged, running three registries

15
00:01:17,668 --> 00:01:23,452
Each registry approves only its own kind of issuer, so a co-op can never mint an ID check

16
00:01:23,602 --> 00:01:32,432
Gaming: Mboa Bet requires 21+, because Cameroon closes betting below civil majority (21)

17
00:01:32,582 --> 00:01:38,585
Manka passes. Ebai, 19, is refused: an adult in many countries, but under 21

18
00:01:38,735 --> 00:01:42,086
Agriculture: Limbe Cocoa Buyers needs proof of current co-op membership, ahead of EU deforestation rules

19
00:01:42,236 --> 00:01:48,720
Fako Cocoa Farmers Union issues; Manka proves. The buyer never sees her name, member number or even her co-op

20
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:54,839
Tabe's good standing was last confirmed 400 days ago: refused until the union renews it

21
00:01:54,989 --> 00:02:03,966
Jobs: Mboa Jobs hires certified solar technicians. Buea Technical Institute is in the Skills registry

22
00:02:04,116 --> 00:02:10,486
A diploma mill that is not accredited tries to issue: rejected. The forgery never enters the registry

23
00:02:10,636 --> 00:02:18,174
One person, three apps, three different nullifiers. Even pooled, their databases do not join

24
00:02:18,324 --> 00:02:23,975
Her three credentials stay on her device; the three public registries hold only hashes and counters

25
00:02:24,325 --> 00:02:28,925
A real Compact contract on Midnight Preprod, a TypeScript SDK and 43 passing tests

26
00:02:29,325 --> 00:02:33,925
The Co-op and Skills registries run in the in-browser simulator for now

27
00:02:34,325 --> 00:02:39,425
Proposed model: apps pay per proof, from 150 FCFA, with 40% going to the issuer

28
00:02:39,825 --> 00:02:44,925
For regulated finance, Kola ID supports CEMAC third-party reliance rather than avoiding it

29
00:02:45,325 --> 00:02:53,925
Go-to-market: one issuer and one app per vertical, starting in Cameroon. Nothing signed yet

30
00:02:54,325 --> 00:03:00,925
Kola ID is an early product with a clear route to market. github.com/mbanyadev/kola-id

